{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The POL-RD-02 arithmetic caps this case. charged_total is SGD 18.05 and the recomputed fare on the booked optimal route is ((3.80 + 0.75 x 9.5 km + 0.28 x 13.0 min) x 1.0, the surge_multiplier read from the fare_breakdown) + 0.80 platform fee = SGD 15.365, giving a refund before rounding of SGD 2.685 and a payable figure of SGD 2.70 rounded UP to the nearest SGD 0.05. That is a refund share of 14.88% of charged_total, far below the 90% which would convert the remedy to FULL_REFUND, and it is SGD 1.30 short of the SGD 4.00 the rider contests. No other line of this fare is reachable.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00303", "EV-TRIP-00303"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.payable",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "On the threshold itself the policy forecloses the driver's own arithmetic, and the driver says so rather than stretch it: trip_record.actual_distance_km is the rounded 11.4 km and may NOT be cited for the threshold test, so the driver's statement that 11.4 against 9.5 is 'exactly 20 percent' does not decide the gate. POL-RD-01 directs the tribunal to gps_trace.trace_distance_km, which is 11.43 km, i.e. 1.93 km and 20.32% over the 9.5 km optimal, so the establishment test is crossed by 0.32 of a percentage point. The driver does not dispute the established excess; the driver's case is that the only consequence the policy attaches to it is the SGD 2.70 set out in the preceding claim.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00303", "EV-TRIP-00303"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The measured excess is 1.93 km and 20.32% of the 9.5 km optimal - past the establishment gate in POL-RD-01 (more than 20% and more than 0.8 km) but far below that clause's materiality gate of 50% or 8.0 km. This is therefore not a MATERIAL deviation, the POL-RD-06 driver_profile check is not engaged, and neither the FULL_REFUND uplift of charged_total nor the POL-RD-06(c) driver-conduct referral is available on this trip's own evidence.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00303", "EV-TRIP-00303"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Even on the discretionary consultation POL-RD-06 permits, no repeat pattern is ESTABLISHED: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 and driver_profile.completed_trips_90d is 260, so the count test (3 or more) fails and the rate test (0.05 or more) fails at 0.00. These are the only two profile fields POL-RD-06 names, and POL-GEN-01 forbids grounding any finding on the lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter or on any other context-only field carried on the artifact.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00303"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-08 puts the initial burden on the rider, and limb (a) requires a matching trip identifier and pickup timestamp across the trip_record, the gps_trace and the fare_breakdown. The fare_breakdown at EV-FARE-00303 carries no pickup timestamp field at all - its only timestamp is charged_at 19:34:43 - so the conjunctive limb (a) showing cannot be completed across all three artifacts on this record, and that element of the rider's initial burden is not documented.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00303", "EV-TRIP-00303", "EV-GPS-00303"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.charged_at",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing may be added on top of the POL-RD-02 figure. The erp_lines are empty and total SGD 0.00, there is no toll line, and the trip neither originates nor ends at an airport (pickup Hougang Mall, dropoff Novena Square), so no POL-RD-09 pass-through correction and no POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity refund arises; POL-RD-09(1) in any event forbids adding off-route ERP on top of the clause 2 amount. The only money that moves on this trip is the distance-and-time recomputation.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00303", "EV-TRIP-00303"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09", "POL-RD-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's filed claim identifies no road, turn, junction or segment and is expressly hedged ('went past the turn i think. not sure. can check?'), and the trip's chat log holds no message at all (message_count 0, first_message_at null), so there is neither a particularised allegation nor a contemporaneous rider complaint on the record for the driver to answer. POL-RD-08 decides the case on cited artifacts and evidence IDs, not on the strength of a recollection.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00303", "EV-TRIP-00303"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}
